docs: keep the rule 18 amendment scaffolding as the audit trail

The three files produced when rule 18 was amended on 2026-10-08 (the
patch, the commit-msg, the apply script) were left in the working tree
untracked. They are not part of the rule change itself, but they are
the only machine-readable record of how the change was applied: the
exact diff, the verbatim commit message, and the apply-and-commit
helper that produced the commit.

Move them into docs/rule-amendments/ so future rule amendments have a
home and so a future agent (or the owner, in six months) reading the
git log can find the patch that produced any rule change in this
repository.

The apply script is updated to point at the new paths so it still
works for future operators who want to re-apply or re-read the patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
